  "stage": "A05 C ABI Python and linear JSON internal mixed power-wave references",
  "base_commit": "828fa197f71908bbc47d45f91449e06ac4c26821",
  "implementation": [
    "C ABI add_power_waves and get_references with transactional errors and capacity/alias checks",
    "Python Network.add_power_waves and reference_impedances_ohms property",
    "Linear JSON constant and sampled per-device reference impedances with strict validation",
    "Parameter model S and embedded Touchstone noise jointly transformed from common reference to local coordinates",
    "Explicit S and intrinsic covariance remain in declared local coordinates, including cross-device correlations",
    "Signal, loaded noise and extracted S/covariance report actual local references; optional output changes preserve boundary coordinates"
  ],
  "independent_checks": [
    "Two ideal S blocks at different real references give analytic 0.6/0.8 scattering and power conservation",
    "Two physical resistors at frequency-dependent internal complex references match uniform-reference physical circuit and S21=0.5",
    "Connection voltages equal, currents opposite, and net power is consistent with RMS V/I",
    "Full cross-device complex rank-one covariance survives global coordinate transformation and internal wiring",
    "Explicit local device covariance is not transformed twice",
    "Touchstone embedded noise and noise figure are invariant under intermediate mixed references",
    "Physical complex internal termination equivalent across local reference choices",
    "C failed additions preserve state/output, invalid/aliased queries preserve outputs and unused capacity tail",
    "Unsupported uniform-reference spectrum entry rejects mixed networks, CLI failed input preserves existing result"
  ],
